armbian-ext4fs
==============

This crate is a vendored fork of `ext4_rs` v1.3.3 by yuoo655
(https://github.com/yuoo655/ext4_rs), distributed under the MIT License.
The original MIT LICENSE is preserved alongside this file.

Modifications made to the upstream source
------------------------------------------

1. Removed the `#![feature(error_in_core)]` nightly feature gate (from
   src/lib.rs and src/prelude.rs). The capability is stable since Rust 1.81,
   so removing the gate lets the crate build on stable Rust.

2. In src/simple_interface/mod.rs, fn `ext4_file_open` now uses
   `InodeFileType::S_IFREG` instead of `S_IFDIR`. The upstream value created
   newly opened files as directories; regular files must be S_IFREG.
   The S_IFDIR values in `ext4_dir_mk` and `ext4_dir_open` are unchanged.
   It also refuses to open anything that is not a regular file.

3. `dir_add_entry` writes the directory entry file type from the child
   inode mode instead of always "directory".

4. `balloc_free_blocks` clears the right bitmap range and walks groups
   correctly; superblock counters are read from disk before each update
   instead of from the snapshot taken at open; truncating to zero frees the
   whole extent tree (any depth) after detaching it from the inode.

5. Directory walks (`dir_find_in_block`, `try_insert_to_existing_block`)
   read entry headers from bytes, skip deleted entries and refuse records
   that would loop or leave the block. Directory block checksums use the
   directory inode instead of the block's first entry, and a block
   allocation without a goal no longer starts at a missing group 1.

The upstream binary (src/main.rs) and its [[bin]] target were removed; only
the library is retained.
